<title>JAPAN: Japan Sept green coffee imports up 18.7 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Sept green coffee imports up 18.7 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's green coffee imports in September totalled 29,181 tonnes, up 18.7 percent from 24,578 tonnes in the same month a year earlier, according to Finance Ministry data released on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Imports of roasted coffee amounted to 488 tonnes in September against 187 tonnes the same month a year earlier.</p>
<p>The breakdown is as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		   Sept 96	   Aug 96	  Sept 95</p>
<p> Total	   29,181	   30,626	   24,578</p>
<p> Indonesia	5,167	    6,302	    5,194</p>
<p> Colombia	 6,572	    6,166	    3,795</p>
<p> Brazil	   6,363	    4,688	    5,720</p>
<p> Guatemala	1,876	    1,779		965</p>
<p> Honduras	 1,173	    1,605	    1,691</p>
<p>Cumulative green coffee imports in the first nine months of 1996 were 242,644 tonnes against 235,639 tonnes in the same period of the previous year.</p>
<p>Roasted coffee imports (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		    Sept 96	  Aug 96	   Sept 95</p>
<p>			 487	   397		 187</p>
</text>
